--TEST--
`prepareRename` on a key of an anonymous object is refused, because the key is no declaration a rename can follow to every read, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $point = {x: 1, y<|>: 2};
echo $point->y, "\n";
--REQUEST--
prepareRename
--EXPECT--
refused: There is nothing to rename here. You can rename a class, a variable, a method, a property, a constant or an enum case.
